---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Claim from '../components/Claim.astro';
import { papers } from '../data/content';
---
<Base title="Research" description="A preprint on detecting silent implementation integrity failures in AI-generated code, and a co-authored conference paper on AI in law.">
  <p class="page-note hand">Papers, and what each one claims.</p>
  <h1 class="page-title">Research</h1>

  <article class="paper">
    <h2>{papers.iia.title}</h2>
    <p class="meta">{papers.iia.authors}. {papers.iia.venue}</p>
    <p>
      A deterministic static analyzer for safety checks that AI-generated Python defines but never runs.
      On a benchmark of <Claim id="iia.scenarios" /> scenarios it reaches MCC <Claim id="iia.mcc" /> against a string-presence
      baseline whose precision and MCC are undefined, because it predicts one class for everything.
      All five errors are reported, with what each one shows about the limits of intra-file analysis.
    </p>
    <ul class="links">
      <li><a href={papers.iia.pdf}>PDF</a></li>
      <li><a href={papers.iia.page}>Project page</a></li>
      <li><a href={papers.iia.code}>Code</a></li>
      <li><a href="/work/integrity-analyzer/">Case study</a></li>
    </ul>
  </article>

  <article class="paper">
    <h2>{papers.law.title}</h2>
    <p class="meta">{papers.law.authors}. {papers.law.venue}</p>
    <p>
      How AI is used in legal research, contract review, e-discovery and online dispute resolution, and how the
      European Union, the United States and India are responding to it, including algorithmic bias and predictive justice.
      I wrote the comparative analysis and the technical sections.
    </p>
    <ul class="links">
      <li><a href={papers.law.pdf}>PDF</a></li>
    </ul>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .page-note {
    font-size: 1.6rem;
    color: var(--yellow);
    margin: 0 0 0.3rem;
    transform: rotate(-2deg);
    transform-origin: left;
    display: inline-block;
  }
  .page-title {
    font-size: clamp(2.1rem, 1.5rem + 3vw, 3.1rem);
    line-height: 1.06;
    letter-spacing: -0.024em;
    font-weight: 750;
    margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
  }
  .paper {
    margin-bottom: 2.4rem;
    padding: 20px 20px 16px;
    background: var(--bg-raised);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: 14px;
  }
  .paper h2 {
    font-size: 1.28rem;
    line-height: 1.32;
    max-width: 42ch;
  }
  .meta {
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    color: var(--text-dim);
    margin: 0.5rem 0 0.9rem;
  }
</style>
